  "text_pages": [
    "Getting around | Univerzita Pardubice\nSkip to main content\nGetting around\nThe University of Pardubice has a centralised campus with a few off-campus buildings nearby. Students walk and ride their bikes between dorms and classes. Those living off-campus ride their bikes or take city buses to class.\nBike\nIf you like cyclying, you'll love Pardubice! The city is flat and bike-friendly with a network of cycling paths. Biking is the fastest way to get around the city.\nBus\nThe city has an exceptional public bus service. Buses go frequently and reach all points in the city. Several buses stop at, or just next to, the University campus. These bus stop names are \"Polabiny, Hradecká\" (buses 3, 7, 17, 33) and \"Univerzita\" (buses 10, 16).\nPardubice city bus schedules are online at\nwww.dpmp.cz\n.\nBuy a bus ticket from the driver when you get onto the bus, or buy them in advance from most convience shops or vending machines. Rechargable bus passes are available online at\nwww.dpmp.cz\n. You can also pay on the bus with your credit card.\nUniversity of Pardubice\nMap\nContacts\n​\nContacts\nFaculties and Central Services and Facilites\nPanoramic view\nExchange/Erasmus+\nInternational students\nMagazine MY UPCE\nWebsite feedback\nServices\nAccommodation\nLibrary\nDepartment of Physical Education and Sports\nNostrification\nE-shop\nThe Centre for Technology  and Knowledge Transfer\nLanguage Centre\nGuidebook for Internationals\nEuropean University Alliance\n© 2023\nUniversity of Pardubice\n,\nStudentská 95\n,\n532 10\nPardubice 2\nPhone:\n+420 466 036 111, 466 036 112, 466 036 113\nWebmaster\n,\nRSS\nData box ID:\nf5vj9hu\nAccessibility Statement\nCC BY-NC-ND 4.0"
